<title>FINLAND: Amer slides on earnings warning.</title>
<headline>Amer slides on earnings warning.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish sporting goods manufacturer Amer-yhtyma Oy fell sharply on Tuesday after the group warned it would remain clearly loss-making in full-year 1996 before extraordinary items and tax, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1530/1230 GMT, Amer traded at 108.00 markka, down six markka or five percent. Volume was moderate at over seven million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;This was to be expected,&quot; one broker said. Amer had already warned it would be loss-making for the full year but had not used the term &quot;clearly&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom + 358 - 0 - 680 50 240</p>
